        "name": "",
        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-12-01T02:08:28.309Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thanks for the insights! I’m fairly new to this system, so I appreciate the wisdom of more experienced GM/players.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"FrivYeti\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"28945\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/48/1919_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> FrivYeti:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is very much running into the “the scene elements are more of an art than a science” part of the game.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, I think this is the key thing that I think I was doing wrong. What the book has to say on Scene Difficulty is really more advice and guidelines rather than hard-and-fast rules that must be obeyed. Right?</p>",
